# Admonitions

Use [Material admonitions](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/admonitions/) for side content that should not break the page flow. `admonition`, `pymdownx.details`, and `pymdownx.superfences` are already enabled. Do not add custom types or extra CSS.

Start a block with `!!!`, a type, and an optional quoted Markdown title. Indent the body by four spaces. Unknown types fall back to `note`. Use only these types: `note`, `abstract`, `info`, `tip`, `success`, `question`, `warning`, `failure`, `danger`, `bug`, `example`, `quote`. Aliases such as `summary` and `tldr` are deprecated.

| Type | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `note` | General aside |
| `info` | Extra context that is not a warning |
| `tip` | A recommended way to write the YAML |
| `warning` | A constraint that is easy to get wrong |
| `failure` / `danger` | Something that will not render or will break the PDF |
| `example` | A short worked snippet beside the main explanation |
| `quote` | A cited remark |

```markdown
!!! warning "Columns and ratio"

    If both `columns` and `ratio` are set, `columns` must equal the length of `ratio`.
```

- Custom title: `!!! tip "Optional title"` after the type. An empty title (`!!! note ""`) drops the icon and title. Empty titles do not work on collapsible blocks.
- Collapsible: `??? note` starts closed. `???+ note` starts open. Prefer these for long optional detail.
- Nested: indent the inner `!!!` block another four spaces inside the outer body.
- Inline sidebar: declare `!!! info inline end "Title"` (right) or `!!! info inline "Title"` (left) *before* the paragraph it sits beside. On narrow viewports it becomes full width.
- Body content can be any Markdown, including lists, tables, and fenced code.
